# Work and trade between residents (Docs/Design/62-talk.md, phase 7): chains. One asks after the other's work, or
# tells their own unasked; the other answers as their trade, their till, their purse and their temper make them; the
# first answers that in kind (work.reply, which reads how the news was told: pair.mem.w7_tone), and some close it.
# Bosses give orders (work.order) or praise (work.praised), and hear pleas for pay (work.plea), for time off
# (work.leave) and worries about the shop (work.worry). Asked at the start of the day, one answers what's ahead
# (work.ahead); at its end, how it went (work.done); asked by their boss, they report (work.report).
#
# The beat that tells the news leaves two things for the reply (pair.mem, half an hour):
#   w7_tone: plain (nothing much), curt (a brush-off), low (the trade going badly), skint (their own money troubles),
#     hard (a hard day: hurt, weather, Restday work), high (the trade going well), good (a good day, or high hopes),
#     tired, busy, idle (a slack spell), bored, proud (denying bad news).
#   w7_from: a or b, who told it (a: told unasked; b: answered a question). With pair.boss this says whether the one
#     replying is the teller's boss or their hand: boss=a and from=b, or boss=b and from=a, is the boss replying.
# Closes: work.end (a plain last word), work.thanks (to kindness or an offer), work.retort (to a jibe).

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- Asking after the work

rule w7_ask_trade
when concept=talk.work|talk.smalltalk pair.band=acquaintances|friends other.business=thriving|steady|failing pair.boss=no
cooldown 1d
say How's trade? | Selling much? | Is the till singing or sulking? | Business keeping you? | Much custom this week?
then other: work.answer

rule w7_ask_trade_close
when concept=talk.work|talk.smalltalk pair.band=friends|family|spouses other.business=thriving|steady|failing self.warmth=warm
cooldown 1d
say And how's business, #pet#? Truly, now. | How's the trade treating you, #pet#? | Tell me straight. How are you doing for custom?
then other: work.answer

rule w7_ask_rival
when concept=talk.work|talk.smalltalk pair.band=rivals other.business=thriving|steady|failing
cooldown 2d
say Still open, are you? | Heard your shelves were full. Nobody buying? | Keeping the doors open, I see. Just.
then other: work.answer

rule w7_ask_workmate
when concept=talk.work other.working=yes pair.boss=no
cooldown 1d
say How's your end going? | Getting anywhere with it? | How's it looking your side? | Making headway?
then other: work.answer

rule w7_ask_chatty
when concept=talk.work|talk.smalltalk self.talk=chatty pair.band=acquaintances|friends other.working=yes
cooldown 2d
say Now then, what are you at? Tell me everything. | Ooh, what's that you're doing? Is it hard? | Don't let me stop you, but how's it all going?
then other: work.answer

## Broad askings: almost anyone, to almost anyone (few criteria, many words)

rule w7_ask_any
when concept=talk.work
cooldown 1d
say How's the work? | Keeping busy? | Much on? | How goes it? | Getting on all right?
then other: work.answer

rule w7_ask_any_day
when concept=talk.work|talk.day here.time=day
cooldown 1d
say Half the day gone already. How's yours? | Got much done? | What's the day thrown at you so far?
then other: work.answer

rule w7_ask_any_friend
when concept=talk.work pair.band=friends|family|spouses
cooldown 1d
say How's it going, #pet#? Really. | Are they working you hard? | Tell me about your day.
then other: work.answer

## Same trade, asking shop talk

rule w7_ask_smith
when concept=talk.work self.job=smith other.job=smith pair.band!=rivals
cooldown 1d
say How's your iron behaving? | Fire drawing well your end? | Many orders in?
then other: work.answer

rule w7_ask_baker
when concept=talk.work self.job=baker other.job=baker pair.band!=rivals
cooldown 1d
say Did your dough rise this morning? Mine sulked. | How's the oven treating you? | Selling out, or feeding the pigeons?
then other: work.answer

rule w7_ask_farmer
when concept=talk.work self.job=farmer other.job=farmer pair.band!=rivals
cooldown 1d
say How's your ground? | Anything coming up your side? | How are the beasts?
then other: work.answer

rule w7_ask_fisher
when concept=talk.work self.job=fisher other.job=fisher
cooldown 1d
say Fish biting for you? | Any luck out there? | How were the nets?
then other: work.answer

rule w7_ask_guard
when concept=talk.work self.role=guard other.role=guard
cooldown 1d
say Quiet on your beat? | Anything doing? | Trouble your way?
then other: work.answer

rule w7_ask_healer
when concept=talk.work self.job=healer other.job=healer
cooldown 1d
say How are your patients? | Many at your door today? | Is that cough still going round your end?
then other: work.answer

rule w7_ask_merchant
when concept=talk.work self.role=merchant other.role=merchant pair.band!=rivals
cooldown 1d
say Moving much? | How's the counting going? | Selling, or just standing?
then other: work.answer

## The start of the day and its end (work.ahead, work.done)

rule w7_ask_before_shift
when concept=talk.work|talk.smalltalk|talk.day other.shift=before
cooldown 1d
say Off to it, then? | Ready for the day? | What's waiting for you today?
then other: work.ahead

rule w7_ask_any_dawn
when concept=talk.work|talk.day here.time=dawn
cooldown 1d
say Up early as ever. Big day? | What's on for today? | You look half asleep. Long day ahead?
then other: work.ahead

rule w7_ask_after_shift
when concept=talk.work|talk.smalltalk|talk.day other.shift=after
cooldown 1d
say Long day? | Finished for the day, then? | How did the day go? | Knocked off at last?
then other: work.done

rule w7_ask_any_dusk
when concept=talk.work|talk.day here.time=dusk|night
cooldown 1d
say Done for the day? | Was it a long one? | Getting home at last?
then other: work.done

## The boss asks how it's going (work.report)

rule w7_ask_boss_checks
when concept=talk.work pair.boss=a other.working=yes self.temper=calm|even
cooldown 1d
say How are you getting on? | All going to plan? | Anything you need from me?
then other: work.report

rule w7_ask_boss_short
when concept=talk.work pair.boss=a other.working=yes self.temper=short|nervy
cooldown 1d
say Is it done yet? | Why's that not finished? | What have you been doing all this while?
then other: work.report

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- Answering about the work (work.answer)

rule w7_ans_plain
when concept=work.answer
say Steady. | Can't grumble. | Same as ever. | Ticking over. | Oh, you know. #work.capitalize#.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_short
when concept=work.answer temper=short
say Busy. Why? | It'd go faster without questions. | Fine. Is that all? | Don't ask.
remember pair: w7_tone=curt 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_merry
when concept=work.answer humour=merry
say Oh, wonderful. Nothing's caught fire yet. | Grand! I've only cursed twice. | Splendid. Ask me again in an hour.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_dry
when concept=work.answer humour=dry
say Thrilling. I can hardly contain myself. | Much as yesterday. And the day before that. | It's #work#. It does what it does.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_guarded
when concept=work.answer honesty=guarded
say Well enough. | Oh, this and that. | It goes. | Can't complain. Wouldn't, if I could.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_ambitious
when concept=work.answer drive=ambitious
say Well, and it'll be better. I've plans. | Good. Not good enough. Not yet. | Growing. You'll see.
remember pair: w7_tone=good 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_content
when concept=work.answer drive=content
say Suits me fine. Always has. | No complaints. The work's honest. | Same as my #dad# had it. That's no bad thing.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_restless
when concept=work.answer drive=restless
say Same as ever. That's the trouble. | I could do it in my sleep. Some days I do. | Dull as ditchwater, if you want the truth.
remember pair: w7_tone=bored 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_quiet
when concept=work.answer talk=quiet
say Fine. | Mm. Good. | Going.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_chatty
when concept=work.answer talk=chatty
say Oh, where to start! First the cart was late, then the cart was early, then... | Busy, busy. Did I tell you about the new stool? It wobbles. | Good! Mostly. You'd not believe the day I've had.
remember pair: w7_tone=busy 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

## The till

rule w7_ans_steady
when concept=work.answer business=steady
say Steady. Pays the rent. | Not rich, not ruined. | Regulars keep me going. | Enough coming in, just.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_failing
when concept=work.answer business=failing
priority 1
say Badly. Nobody's buying. | Four days without a sale. I've started counting flies. | I'll be shut by the next moon, the way it's going. | I count the till and it doesn't take long.
remember pair: w7_tone=low 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_thriving
when concept=work.answer business=thriving
priority 1
say Run off my paws! | Can't keep the shelves full. | Best month I've had. Touch wood. | I've a waiting list. Me!
remember pair: w7_tone=high 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_failing_proud
when concept=work.answer business=failing temper=short warmth=cold|reserved
priority 1
say Fine. It's fine. | Never better. | It'll pick up. It always picks up. | Mind your own till.
remember pair: w7_tone=proud 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_thriving_guarded
when concept=work.answer business=thriving honesty=guarded|sly
priority 1
say Oh, slow. Terribly slow. | Mustn't grumble. | Getting by, getting by.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_owes
when concept=work.answer owes=yes business=steady|failing
priority 1
say I'm working for the lender, not for me. | Everything I take goes out the door again. Debts. | I'd be fine if I didn't owe half the street.
remember pair: w7_tone=low 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_destitute
when concept=work.answer wealth=destitute
priority 2
say I'm working and still can't eat. Tell me how that's right. | There isn't enough work in the world to dig me out. | Every penny's gone before I've earned it.
remember pair: w7_tone=skint 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_tired
when concept=work.answer tired=yes working=yes
priority 1
say I'm asleep on my paws. | #tired.capitalize#. Ask me after I've slept. | Long. Very long. And not done yet. | I could lie down on this floor.
remember pair: w7_tone=tired 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_before
when concept=work.answer shift=before
say Not started. Don't remind me. | Off to it now. Wish me luck. | Ask me tonight.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_after
when concept=work.answer shift=after
say Done for the day, and glad of it. | Finished. Feet up soon. | It's behind me now. That's the best part.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_day_off
when concept=work.answer shift=day_off
say Not today! Day off. Don't spoil it. | I'm not thinking about it. Not one thought. | Ask me tomorrow. Today I'm a wolf of leisure.
remember pair: w7_tone=good 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_hurt
when concept=work.answer injured=light working=yes
priority 1
say Working one-pawed today. Took a knock. | Slower than usual. It's the shoulder. | Fine, if I don't lift anything. Which is the whole job.
remember pair: w7_tone=hard 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

## The day's kind

rule w7_ans_market_merchant
when concept=work.answer here.day=market role=merchant
priority 1
say Market day! Don't ask me now. | Haven't sat since dawn. | Everyone wants everything, and all at once.
remember pair: w7_tone=busy 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_market_food
when concept=work.answer here.day=market job=baker|cook|brewer|innkeeper
priority 1
say Market day. Cleared out by noon, I'll be. | Feeding half the county today. | Every stallholder wants feeding and every farmer wants a drink.
remember pair: w7_tone=busy 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_restday
when concept=work.answer here.day=rest working=yes
priority 1
say Working Restday. Again. | Restday, they call it. Not for me. | Somebody has to.
remember pair: w7_tone=hard 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_festival
when concept=work.answer here.day=festival working=yes
priority 1
say Working through the festival. Can you hear them out there? | Everyone's dancing but me. | Feast days are work days, for some of us.
remember pair: w7_tone=hard 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

## Masters, apprentices, the Houses

rule w7_ans_apprentice
when concept=work.answer apprentice=yes
say Learning. Slowly. | I've ruined less than yesterday. | My master says I'm improving. Then sighs.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_master
when concept=work.answer master=yes
say Good, but the apprentice will be the death of me. | Teaching takes twice as long as doing. | Well. My pupil's coming on.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_house
when concept=work.answer self.house job!=noble
say The House keeps us busy. | Steady. The House always has work. Pays when it pays. | Can't complain. It's House work. Regular.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_greatly
when concept=work.answer self.house=greatly_house working=yes job!=noble
say Brick, lime, brick, lime. Greatly sells and I carry. | Another load of tiles for the Greatly Yard. My shoulders know every one. | Greatly's paint in my fur again. Never comes out.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_fell
when concept=work.answer self.house=house_fell working=yes job!=noble
say Sawdust in everything. House Fell's got orders stacked to the roof. | Planks, staves, wheels. Fell wants all of it yesterday. | Timber's wet. Fell says cut it anyway.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_grayrock
when concept=work.answer self.house=grayrock_hall working=yes job!=noble
say Grayrock's furnaces don't sleep. Nor do we, much. | Iron in, iron out. Grayrock counts every bar. | Hot, loud, and Grayrock's steward watching.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_mossgrave
when concept=work.answer self.house=mossgrave_court working=yes job!=noble
say Dye to the elbows. Mossgrave blue, this week. | The tannery stinks and Mossgrave pays. That's the deal. | Wool, wool and more wool. Mossgrave's never short of sheep.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

## By trade

rule w7_ans_smith
when concept=work.answer job=smith
say Iron's poor this month. Brittle. | Hinges, nails, hinges. Never a sword. | Singed the same paw three times. Otherwise good.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_baker
when concept=work.answer job=baker
say Up since the small hours. | Dough sulked this morning, but it came round. | Flour in my ears, flour in my fur. Same as ever.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_brewer
when concept=work.answer job=brewer
say The new batch is working. You can smell it from the street. | Barrels to scrub. Always barrels to scrub. | Good brew this time. Don't tell anyone.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_innkeeper
when concept=work.answer job=innkeeper
say Full last night, and not one of them paid on time. | Rooms let, stools broken. A good week. | The cellar's full and the taproom's empty. Wrong way round.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_guard
when concept=work.answer role=guard
say Quiet. I like quiet. | Two drunks and a lost goat. | Boots wearing through. Otherwise fine.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_soldier
when concept=work.answer job=soldier
say Drill, polish, drill. | They march us up the hill and march us down again. | Waiting. Soldiering's mostly waiting.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_farmer
when concept=work.answer job=farmer
say The ground's good, if the sky behaves. | Weeds grow faster than I can pull them. | Beasts are fed. That's a day.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_farmer_spring
when concept=work.answer job=farmer here.season=spring
priority 1
say Sowing. My back's in two pieces. | Seed's in. Now we wait and pray. | Ploughing till dark, every day.
remember pair: w7_tone=busy 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_farmer_summer
when concept=work.answer job=farmer here.season=summer
priority 1
say Haymaking. Every dry day counts. | Hoeing. Endless hoeing. | Watching the sky and the barley, both.
remember pair: w7_tone=busy 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_farmer_autumn
when concept=work.answer job=farmer here.season=autumn
priority 1
say Harvest. Talk to me when it's in the barn. | Every paw in the field and still not enough. | Good yield this year. Or it will be, if the rain holds off.
remember pair: w7_tone=busy 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_farmer_winter
when concept=work.answer job=farmer here.season=winter
priority 1
say Mending fences and staring at the snow. | Winter. Nothing to do but feed the beasts and worry. | Sharpening everything I own, twice.
remember pair: w7_tone=idle 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_herder
when concept=work.answer job=herder
say Flock's well. One wanders, but there's always one. | Counted them twice. Same number both times. | Ewes are fat and the shepherds are lazy.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_herder_spring
when concept=work.answer job=herder here.season=spring
priority 1
say Lambing. I've not slept in a week. | Twins in the night, both living. | Up to my elbows in ewe. Don't shake my paw.
remember pair: w7_tone=tired 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_herder_winter
when concept=work.answer job=herder here.season=winter
priority 1
say Hay's going faster than I'd like. | Brought them all down off the hill before the snow. | Breaking ice on the troughs every morning.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_fisher
when concept=work.answer job=fisher
say Nets came up half full. Or half empty, depending who's counting. | Fish are deep today. Sulking, like the rest of us. | Good catch. Smell my paws if you don't believe me.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_fisher_storm
when concept=work.answer job=fisher here.weather=storm|fog
priority 1
say No boats out in this. Not mine, anyway. | Sat on the shore mending nets and watching the water. | I'll not argue with water like this.
remember pair: w7_tone=idle 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_miner
when concept=work.answer job=miner
say Seam's thinning. | Dark and wet and the lamp keeps guttering. Normal, then. | Brought up good ore today. My back paid for it.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_healer
when concept=work.answer job=healer
say Coughs, cuts and one broken tail. | Busy. Everyone's ill at once, as usual. | Lost none today. That's a good day.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_healer_winter
when concept=work.answer job=healer here.season=winter
priority 1
say Coughs. Every chest in town is rattling. | Chilblains and fevers, door to door. | I've run out of willow bark twice this week.
remember pair: w7_tone=busy 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_priest
when concept=work.answer job=priest
say The chapel's full on Restday and empty the rest. | Two weddings to plan and one burial. | The roof leaks on the altar. I'm told it's a test.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_scholar
when concept=work.answer job=scholar
say I've read the same page eleven times. | Ink's run out and so has my patience. | I found an error in a book two hundred years old. Wonderful day.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_laborer
when concept=work.answer job=laborer
say Carried things from there to here. Tomorrow, from here to there. | Shoulders aching. Pay's coming, they say. | Work's work. It's #money#.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_carter
when concept=work.answer job=carter
say Road's rutted to the axle. | Mule's in a mood, I'm in a mood. | Two loads today and a wheel that squeals.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_crafter
when concept=work.answer job=crafter
say Three orders, and every one wanted yesterday. | Steady paws, steady work. | Spoiled a piece this morning. Started again.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_servant
when concept=work.answer job=servant
say The mistress has changed her mind about the curtains. Again. | Fetch, carry, polish, smile. | Silver's polished. The family's not.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_servant_heights
when concept=work.answer job=servant quarter=heights
priority 1
say Three dinners this week. Thirty guests. One of me. | They've guests from the other Houses. Everything has to shine. | The young master's back from the south. Bright One help us.
remember pair: w7_tone=busy 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_cook
when concept=work.answer job=cook
say Burnt the onions, saved the stew. | The pot's been on since dawn. | Everyone wants feeding and nobody wants to pay.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_woodcutter
when concept=work.answer job=woodcutter
say Felled two and split one. | Axe needs grinding. So do I. | The wood's wet and so am I.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_official
when concept=work.answer job=official
say Paper. Mountains of it. | Three petitions, two complaints and a lost seal. | Every wolf in town wants a stamp on something.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_sailor
when concept=work.answer job=sailor
say Ashore till the cargo's loaded. I'm climbing the walls. | Rigging to mend, decks to scrub. | Good wind coming. We'll be off soon.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_beggar
when concept=work.answer job=beggar
say Three pennies and a crust. Good day, for me. | Folk walk faster when they see me. | It's a trade like any other. Worse pay.
remember pair: w7_tone=skint 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_merchant
when concept=work.answer role=merchant
say Buying cheap, selling dear, or trying to. | The counting's the hard part. | Customers come in waves. Today's a dry tide.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_noble
when concept=work.answer job=noble
say Work? I sign things. Then I sign other things. | The steward does the work. I do the worrying. | Petitions, accounts, and a cousin who wants money.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_young
when concept=work.answer stage=young
say I fed the hens! All of them! | I carried a bucket all the way without spilling. Mostly. | I'm helping. #mum# says I'm helping.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

## A trade and its till: the specific news

rule w7_ans_smith_failing
when concept=work.answer job=smith business=failing
priority 1
say Forge is cold half the day. No orders. | Nobody's mending anything. They're making do. | I've more hinges on the shelf than doors in town.
remember pair: w7_tone=low 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_smith_thriving
when concept=work.answer job=smith business=thriving
priority 1
say Orders till the month's end. Can't hammer fast enough. | Hinges, blades, shoes. The anvil hasn't been quiet in days. | Good iron and good custom. Mark the day.
remember pair: w7_tone=high 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_baker_failing
when concept=work.answer job=baker business=failing
priority 1
say Yesterday's loaves are today's loaves. And tomorrow's. | Baked forty, sold twelve. | They're buying from the other one. Cheaper, they say.
remember pair: w7_tone=low 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_baker_thriving
when concept=work.answer job=baker business=thriving
priority 1
say Sold out by mid-morning. Every day this week. | They queue in the dark for my loaves now. | Another oven, that's what I need.
remember pair: w7_tone=high 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_brewer_failing
when concept=work.answer job=brewer business=failing
priority 1
say Barrels full, purse empty. | The inns are buying elsewhere. | I'll be drinking my own stock at this rate. All of it.
remember pair: w7_tone=low 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_brewer_thriving
when concept=work.answer job=brewer business=thriving
priority 1
say Every barrel spoken for before it's tapped. | The town's thirsty and I'm the well. | Can't brew it fast enough. Lovely problem.
remember pair: w7_tone=high 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_inn_failing
when concept=work.answer job=innkeeper business=failing
priority 1
say Empty rooms. Empty stools. Full cellar. | One guest all week, and he left without paying. | The fire's lit for nobody.
remember pair: w7_tone=low 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_inn_thriving
when concept=work.answer job=innkeeper business=thriving
priority 1
say Every bed taken. I've had them sleeping on the benches. | Can't pour fast enough. | Full house every night. My feet hate me.
remember pair: w7_tone=high 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_merchant_failing
when concept=work.answer role=merchant business=failing
priority 1
say Stock's gathering dust. I could sell the dust. | Folk look, folk touch, folk leave. | I've cut my prices to the bone and still nothing.
remember pair: w7_tone=low 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_merchant_thriving
when concept=work.answer role=merchant business=thriving
priority 1
say Sold out of half the stock. Waiting on the carts. | Couldn't be better. Don't tell my rivals. | I'm thinking of a second stall.
remember pair: w7_tone=high 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_crafter_failing
when concept=work.answer job=crafter business=failing
priority 1
say Made it beautiful, and nobody wants beautiful. | No orders. I'm making things for the shelf now. | Folk mend their old ones instead.
remember pair: w7_tone=low 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_cook_thriving
when concept=work.answer job=cook|innkeeper business=thriving here.day=market|festival
priority 1
say The pot's emptied twice already. | Fed two hundred if I fed one. | Out of bread, out of stew, still they come.
remember pair: w7_tone=busy 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- What's ahead today (work.ahead)

rule w7_ahead_plain
when concept=work.ahead
say Same as yesterday, I expect. | Oh, the usual. | Whatever comes through the door. | A day's work, same as any.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ahead_short
when concept=work.ahead temper=short
say It'll be longer for standing here. | Work. What else? | If folk let me get to it.
remember pair: w7_tone=curt 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ahead_tired
when concept=work.ahead tired=yes
priority 1
say I've not woken up yet. Ask me later. | Long. They're all long. | My eyes are open. The rest of me's in #bed#.
remember pair: w7_tone=tired 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ahead_day_off
when concept=work.ahead shift=day_off
priority 1
say Nothing! Day off. | Not a thing. I'm off today, and I mean off. | A long sit and a short walk. Day off.
remember pair: w7_tone=good 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ahead_at_it
when concept=work.ahead working=yes shift=during
say Ahead? I've been at it since first light. | Already halfway through it. | I'm in the middle of it now. Look.
remember pair: w7_tone=busy 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ahead_failing
when concept=work.ahead business=failing
priority 1
say Opening up. For all the good it'll do. | Sitting behind the counter, waiting. Same as yesterday. | Dusting stock nobody buys.
remember pair: w7_tone=low 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ahead_thriving
when concept=work.ahead business=thriving
priority 1
say Opening early. They'll be queuing. | Three orders before noon, and more coming. | A full day. A good full day.
remember pair: w7_tone=high 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ahead_market
when concept=work.ahead here.day=market role=merchant
priority 1
say Market day. The biggest of the week. | Setting out the stall before the crowd comes. | Market. I'll not sit down till dark.
remember pair: w7_tone=busy 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ahead_restless
when concept=work.ahead drive=restless
say The same as every day. Every single day. | What's ahead? The same as behind. | Nothing I haven't done a thousand times.
remember pair: w7_tone=bored 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ahead_ambitious
when concept=work.ahead drive=ambitious
say A big order to finish, and a bigger one to win. | Today I talk to the steward about the contract. | More than yesterday. That's the plan, every day.
remember pair: w7_tone=good 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ahead_farmer
when concept=work.ahead job=farmer|herder
say The beasts first. Then whatever the sky allows. | Fences, ditches, and a gate that won't shut. | Out to the far field, if the ground's dry.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ahead_farmer_autumn
when concept=work.ahead job=farmer here.season=autumn
priority 1
say Harvest. Every paw we've got. | Cutting the low field before the rain. | Sheaves, sheaves and more sheaves.
remember pair: w7_tone=busy 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ahead_baker
when concept=work.ahead job=baker
say Ahead? The baking's done. I've been up since the dark. | Selling what I baked in the night. | The second batch, then the third.
remember pair: w7_tone=busy 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ahead_fisher
when concept=work.ahead job=fisher
say Out on the water, if it stays calm. | Nets, boat, and whatever swims into them. | The early tide. I'm late already.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ahead_fisher_storm
when concept=work.ahead job=fisher here.weather=storm|fog
priority 1
say Not going out in this. Nets to mend instead. | Sitting on the shore and glaring at the water. | Nothing. The water's decided for me.
remember pair: w7_tone=idle 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ahead_miner
when concept=work.ahead job=miner
say Down the hole. Same as ever. | Dark, then darker, then home. | The new drift, if it's not flooded.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ahead_guard
when concept=work.ahead role=guard
say The gate till dusk. | Walking the wall, round and round. | Whatever the captain hasn't thought of yet.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ahead_healer
when concept=work.ahead job=healer
say Whoever's ill. I'll know when they knock. | Three calls to make, and the poultices to mix. | A birth, if it comes today. It might.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ahead_innkeeper
when concept=work.ahead job=innkeeper|cook
say Bread to set, beds to strip, and a cellar to count. | Feeding whoever walks in. | A pot of stew the size of a cart.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ahead_apprentice
when concept=work.ahead apprentice=yes
say Whatever my master thinks of. Sweeping, likely. | I'm to try it on my own today. On my own! | Fetching and carrying. Learning, they call it.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ahead_young
when concept=work.ahead stage=young
say Helping! I'm helping #mum#. | Fetching water, and then playing. Mostly playing. | Feeding the hens. They peck.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- How did the day go (work.done)

rule w7_done_plain
when concept=work.done
say Long enough. | Long, but it's over. | Oh, it went. They do.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_done_still
when concept=work.done shift=during
priority 1
say Done? I wish. Another hour, at least. | Not yet. Not nearly. | Nearly. Not nearly enough.
remember pair: w7_tone=hard 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_done_after
when concept=work.done shift=after
say Over and done. Boots off soon. | Finished, and not a moment too soon. | Behind me, where it belongs.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_done_day_off
when concept=work.done shift=day_off
priority 1
say Done? I never started. Day off! | Not a stroke of work all day. Lovely. | I've been idle since dawn and I'm proud of it.
remember pair: w7_tone=good 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_done_tired
when concept=work.done tired=yes shift=after|none
priority 1
say Done in. #bed.capitalize#'s calling. | I've nothing left. Not a whisker. | Over. Thank the gods it's over.
remember pair: w7_tone=tired 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_done_short
when concept=work.done temper=short
say Long. Don't make it longer. | It went. Like they all go. | Don't ask.
remember pair: w7_tone=curt 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_done_merry
when concept=work.done humour=merry
say Long! I've aged a year. Look, grey whiskers. | Marvellous. I only broke one thing. | I survived it. Someone ring a bell.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_done_failing
when concept=work.done business=failing
priority 1
say Long, and nothing to show for it. | Two customers. Two. | I sat and watched the door all day.
remember pair: w7_tone=low 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_done_thriving
when concept=work.done business=thriving
priority 1
say Long, and every hour of it paid. | Sold out by afternoon. Again. | Good. Very good. Tired, but good.
remember pair: w7_tone=high 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_done_innkeeper
when concept=work.done job=innkeeper here.time=dusk|night
priority 1
say Done? The night's when my work starts. | They're only just coming in. Ask me at closing. | Done? I've a full taproom.
remember pair: w7_tone=busy 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_done_farmer
when concept=work.done job=farmer|herder
say The beasts are in and the gate's shut. | Fields to the hedge, and every beast fed. | Done, till the cows say otherwise.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_done_smith
when concept=work.done job=smith
say Fire's banked. My arms are lead. | Forty nails and a gate. Fair day. | Done. I'll hear the anvil in my sleep.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_done_miner
when concept=work.done job=miner
say Up out of the dark, at last. | Out, and every one of us with me. That's a good day. | I'll be coughing up the seam till morning.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_done_fisher
when concept=work.done job=fisher
say Nets hung, boat's up. | Wet through, but the boat's full. | The water gave a little. It'll do.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_done_guard
when concept=work.done role=guard
say Watch handed over. Quiet one. | Boots off soon. Best part of the day. | Nobody stabbed. I'll call that good.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_done_baker
when concept=work.done job=baker
say I finished at noon. I start in the dark, remember. | Long done. I'll be asleep before the lamps are lit. | Done since midday. Up again in the small hours.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_done_healer
when concept=work.done job=healer
say Done, unless someone knocks in the night. They will. | Seven calls and one birth. | Done for now. Healers are never done.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_done_old
when concept=work.done stage=old
say Long. They're all long now. | My knees say it was longer than it was. | Done. I'll sit, and I'll not get up again till morning.
remember pair: w7_tone=tired 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_done_young
when concept=work.done stage=young
say I played all day! Was that work? | I helped! I helped all day! | It was long. Is it nearly #supper#?
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- Answering the boss (work.report)

rule w7_rpt_plain
when concept=work.report
say Getting there. | Nearly done, I promise. | On it. Right on it. | Going well. Honest.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_rpt_tired
when concept=work.report tired=yes
priority 1
say Fine! Fine. Not tired at all. | Wide awake. Never better. *yawns* | Going well. Why, do I look tired?
remember pair: w7_tone=tired 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_rpt_short
when concept=work.report temper=short
say It'll be done when it's done. | Faster if you'd stop asking. | I've two paws. Not four.
remember pair: w7_tone=curt 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_rpt_ambitious
when concept=work.report drive=ambitious
say Done, and I've started the next. | Finished early. Give me more. | Done. Have you thought about what I said? More hours?
remember pair: w7_tone=good 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_rpt_sly
when concept=work.report honesty=sly
say Nearly. Very nearly. Practically done. | Coming along beautifully. Don't look yet. | Done. Well. Done-ish.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_rpt_nervy
when concept=work.report temper=nervy
say Is something wrong? I'm going as fast as I can. | Sorry! Nearly. Sorry. | I think it's right. Is it right?
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_rpt_merry
when concept=work.report humour=merry
say Done? It's practically a work of art. | Going so well I've frightened myself. | Nearly, and only a little bit wonky.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_rpt_quiet
when concept=work.report talk=quiet
say Nearly. | Mm. Soon. | Going.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_rpt_hurt
when concept=work.report injured=light
priority 1
say Slower than I'd like. It's the shoulder. | Doing it one-pawed. It's taking a while. | Getting there. Carefully.
remember pair: w7_tone=hard 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_rpt_apprentice
when concept=work.report apprentice=yes
say Like this? I think it's right this time. | I've done it twice. The second's better. | Nearly, master. I only spoiled one.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_rpt_young
when concept=work.report stage=young|adolescent
say Nearly! Don't look yet! | I did it all myself. Mostly. | Is it meant to look like that?
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=b 30m
then other: work.reply

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- Replying to what the other said (work.reply)

## Nothing much

rule w7_rep_plain
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=plain
say Same as ever, then. | Aye, it goes. | Ah, well. | Isn't it always the way. | That's #work# for you.

rule w7_rep_plain_chatty
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=plain talk=chatty
say Oh, I know just what you mean. Mine's the same. Let me tell you... | Isn't it always! My cousin says the same. | Same here, same here. Did you hear about the miller?

rule w7_rep_plain_dry
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=plain humour=dry
say Riveting. | Stop, I can't take the excitement. | I'll write it in my book of wonders.

rule w7_rep_plain_young
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=plain stage=young
say When I'm big I'm going to do that too. | Can I help? I'm good at helping. | Is it hard? It looks hard.

rule w7_rep_plain_boss
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=plain pair.boss=a pair.mem.w7_from=b
say Good. Keep at it. | Right. Shout if you need me. | Mind you do it properly.
then other: work.end

rule w7_rep_plain_boss_told
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=plain pair.boss=b pair.mem.w7_from=a
say Good. Keep at it. | Right. Shout if you need me. | Mind you do it properly.
then other: work.end

## A brush-off

rule w7_rep_curt
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=curt
say All right. Only asking. | Sorry I spoke. | Suit yourself.

rule w7_rep_curt_warm
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=curt warmth=warm
say Bad day? I'll leave you be. | All right, #pet#. Later, then. | I'll not keep you. Chin up.

rule w7_rep_curt_short
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=curt temper=short
say Bite my head off, then. | Charming. | Next time I'll not bother.

rule w7_rep_curt_boss
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=curt pair.boss=a pair.mem.w7_from=b
say Mind your tone. | Less lip, more work. | I'll ask as often as I like. I pay you.
then other: work.end

## The trade going badly

rule w7_rep_low
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=low
say I'm sorry to hear it. | That's hard. | It'll turn. These things do. | #oath#. That's no good.

rule w7_rep_low_warm
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=low warmth=warm
say If it comes to the worst, you come to me first. You hear? | Oh, #pet#. I'll send folk your way. See if I don't. | Don't carry it alone. Come by tonight.
then other: work.thanks

rule w7_rep_low_cold
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=low warmth=cold
say Hm. Well, that's trade. | Some do, some don't. | Then work harder.
then other: work.retort

rule w7_rep_low_rival
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=low pair.band=rivals
say Is it? Shame. | Oh dear. Oh dear, oh dear. | I'd offer to help, but you'd only refuse.
then other: work.retort

rule w7_rep_low_thriving
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=low business=thriving
say Mine's doing well, if that helps. It doesn't, does it. | Odd. My till's never been fuller. | Funny, I can't keep up. Want my overflow?

rule w7_rep_low_failing
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=low business=failing
say Mine too. It's the whole town. | You and me both. Nobody's spending. | Don't. I could have said the same word for word.

rule w7_rep_low_poor
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=low wealth=poor|destitute
say Join the club. Plenty of room. | We're all scraping, #address#. | Welcome to my life.

rule w7_rep_low_rich
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=low wealth=rich warmth=warm
say If it's a matter of #money#, come and see me. Quietly. | I could put something your way. No, I mean it. | Let me buy a few things. It's no charity, I need them.
then other: work.thanks

rule w7_rep_low_devout
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=low piety=devout
say I'll say a word for you on Restday. | The Bright One sees honest work. Truly. | The Bright One's seen worse turn round.

rule w7_rep_low_dry
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=low humour=dry
say Could be worse. You could be me. | Well, the rats will be pleased. | At least it's quiet.

rule w7_rep_low_merry
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=low humour=merry
say Chin up! Worse things happen at sea. I've seen them. | You'll laugh about it in a year. I'll laugh now, to save time. | Sell me something, then. Anything. I'll wear it.

rule w7_rep_low_ambitious
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=low drive=ambitious
say Then change something. Sell something else. | Move the stall. Lower the price. Shout louder. | Sitting still is how shops die.
then other: work.end

rule w7_rep_low_old
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=low stage=old
say I've seen worse years. You'll come through. | It was the same when I was your age. It passed. | Lean years and fat years. Hold on.

rule w7_rep_low_hand
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=low pair.boss=b pair.mem.w7_from=b
say Does that mean... are my #wages# safe? | Should I be looking for other work? | We'll pull through. Won't we?
then other: work.worry

rule w7_rep_low_hand_told
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=low pair.boss=a pair.mem.w7_from=a
say Does that mean... are my #wages# safe? | Should I be looking for other work? | We'll pull through. Won't we?
then other: work.worry

## Their own money troubles

rule w7_rep_skint
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=skint
say That's not right. It's not. | Hard times. | #oath#, that's grim. | Something'll turn up. It has to.

rule w7_rep_skint_warm
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=skint warmth=warm wealth=comfortable|rich
say Come and eat with us tonight. No arguing. | Here. Take this. No, take it. | You'll not go hungry while I've a pot on.
then other: work.thanks

rule w7_rep_skint_poor
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=skint wealth=poor|destitute
say Same boat, #address#. Same leaky boat. | Don't I know it. | I'd lend you some if I had some.

rule w7_rep_skint_devout
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=skint piety=devout
say The chapel has bread for them that ask. No shame in it. | I'll pray for you. And bring you a loaf. | The Bright One hasn't forgotten you. Nor have I.

rule w7_rep_skint_cold
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=skint warmth=cold
say Then find better work. | Should've saved, then. | Everyone's short. You're not special.
then other: work.retort

rule w7_rep_skint_dry
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=skint humour=dry
say Money's like that. Never where you are. | They say it's the root of all evil. I'd risk it. | At least nobody's robbing you. Nothing to rob.

rule w7_rep_skint_boss
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=skint pair.boss=a pair.mem.w7_from=b
say I pay what I can. You know that. | Don't look at me like that. I pay fair. | Come and see me after. We'll see.
then other: work.end

rule w7_rep_skint_boss_told
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=skint pair.boss=b pair.mem.w7_from=a
say I pay what I can. You know that. | Don't look at me like that. I pay fair. | Come and see me after. We'll see.
then other: work.end

## A hard day

rule w7_rep_hard
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=hard
say Rough day, then. | That's hard luck. | Some days are like that. | It'll be better tomorrow.

rule w7_rep_hard_warm
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=hard warmth=warm
say Sit a minute. I'll fetch you something. | Here, let me take a turn. | Come by after. There's a fire and a drop of something.
then other: work.thanks

rule w7_rep_hard_merry
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=hard humour=merry
say Tomorrow can't be worse. Probably. | Look at it this way. No, there's no good way. | Cheer up. Then fall down. Then cheer up again.

rule w7_rep_hard_dry
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=hard humour=dry
say Some days the world has it in for you. | Well, you're still standing. Roughly. | Could be worse. I don't see how, mind.

rule w7_rep_hard_old
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=hard stage=old
say At my age every day's like that. | You'll mend. We always mend. | I had forty years of days like that. They pass.

rule w7_rep_hard_tired
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=hard tired=yes
say You and me both. | Don't. I've had the same. | We're a sorry pair today.

rule w7_rep_hard_boss_warm
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=hard pair.boss=a pair.mem.w7_from=b warmth=warm
say Go easy the rest of today. | Leave the heavy work. I'll find someone. | Take it slow. I'd rather slow than broken.
then other: work.thanks

rule w7_rep_hard_boss_warm_told
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=hard pair.boss=b pair.mem.w7_from=a warmth=warm
say Go easy the rest of today. | Leave the heavy work. I'll find someone. | Take it slow. I'd rather slow than broken.
then other: work.thanks

rule w7_rep_hard_boss_cold
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=hard pair.boss=a pair.mem.w7_from=b warmth=cold
say Work's work. Get on with it. | We all have days. | I don't pay for hard days. I pay for done ones.
then other: work.end

rule w7_rep_hard_boss_cold_told
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=hard pair.boss=b pair.mem.w7_from=a warmth=cold
say Work's work. Get on with it. | We all have days. | I don't pay for hard days. I pay for done ones.
then other: work.end

## The trade going well

rule w7_rep_high
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=high
say Glad to hear it. | Long may it last. | Well! Somebody's doing well. | Good. Somebody ought to be.

rule w7_rep_high_poor
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=high wealth=poor|destitute
say Must be nice. | Good for some. | Spare a thought for the rest of us.

rule w7_rep_high_failing
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=high business=failing
say While mine starves. Lovely. | Glad someone's selling. | Teach me, then. Go on.

rule w7_rep_high_rival
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=high pair.band=rivals
say Luck. It won't last. | Funny. I heard different. | Enjoy it. Fashions change.
then other: work.retort

rule w7_rep_high_sly
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=high honesty=sly
say Drinks are on you, then. | So you'll not miss a penny or two. | Remember your friends, eh? Me, specifically.

rule w7_rep_high_ambitious
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=high drive=ambitious
say Whatever you're doing, I'll be doing it next week. | Lucky. I'll make my own. | Hm. I'll have to have a look at your stall.

rule w7_rep_high_warm
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=high warmth=warm
say Oh, that's lovely. You've earned it. | Oh, that warms me through. | Good! I've been hoping it'd come right.

rule w7_rep_high_devout
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=high piety=devout
say Thank the Bright One for it. And tithe, mind. | Blessings come to honest paws. | Don't forget the chapel box.

rule w7_rep_high_hand
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=high pair.boss=b pair.mem.w7_from=b
say Then a little extra in my #wages# wouldn't hurt? | Good. So you'll be wanting more help? | And who sold most of it, I wonder?
then other: work.plea

rule w7_rep_high_hand_told
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=high pair.boss=a pair.mem.w7_from=a
say Then a little extra in my #wages# wouldn't hurt? | Good. So you'll be wanting more help? | And who sold most of it, I wonder?
then other: work.plea

## A good day, or high hopes

rule w7_rep_good
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=good
say Good for you. | Well, there's a thing. | Hold on to that. | I'll drink to that.

rule w7_rep_good_poor
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=good wealth=poor|destitute
say Wish mine went like that. | Some of us get the other sort. | Lucky you.

rule w7_rep_good_warm
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=good warmth=warm
say That's lovely to hear. | You deserve it. You do. | Ha! Look at you, all pleased.

rule w7_rep_good_dry
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=good humour=dry
say Mark the day. Somebody's happy. | Don't say it too loud. The gods listen. | Enjoy it. It never lasts.

rule w7_rep_good_old
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=good stage=old
say Ah, I remember being like that. | Good. Make the most of it while your knees work. | That's the spirit. Keep it.

rule w7_rep_good_boss
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=good pair.boss=a pair.mem.w7_from=b
say Good. Then I've more for you. | Glad to hear it. Don't let it go to your head. | We'll see. Show me tomorrow too.
then other: work.end

rule w7_rep_good_boss_told
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=good pair.boss=b pair.mem.w7_from=a
say Good. Then I've more for you. | Glad to hear it. Don't let it go to your head. | We'll see. Show me tomorrow too.
then other: work.end

## Tired

rule w7_rep_tired
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=tired
say You look it. | Get some rest when you can. | Go easy on yourself. | Don't fall asleep on your paws.

rule w7_rep_tired_old
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=tired stage=old other.stage=young|adolescent|adult
say Try it at my age. | You're young. You'll bounce. | I remember being that tired. Now I'm just old.

rule w7_rep_tired_tired
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=tired tired=yes
say You and me both. | Don't talk to me about tired. | We'll sleep standing, like horses.

rule w7_rep_tired_merry
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=tired humour=merry
say Sleep's for the rich and the dead. | I'll prop you up with a broom. | Lie down in the cart. Nobody'll notice.

rule w7_rep_tired_warm
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=tired warmth=warm pair.boss=no
say Sit a moment. Go on. | Here, lean on me a bit. | Go to #bed# early tonight. Promise me.
then other: work.thanks

rule w7_rep_tired_boss_warm
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=tired pair.boss=a pair.mem.w7_from=b warmth=warm
say Then finish that and get home. I'll manage. | Go on, knock off early. Just today. | Sit down a moment. The work will wait.
then other: work.thanks

rule w7_rep_tired_boss_warm_told
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=tired pair.boss=b pair.mem.w7_from=a warmth=warm
say Then finish that and get home. I'll manage. | Go on, knock off early. Just today. | Sit down a moment. The work will wait.
then other: work.thanks

rule w7_rep_tired_boss_cold
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=tired pair.boss=a pair.mem.w7_from=b warmth=cold
say Tired? There's an hour yet. | I don't pay you to yawn. | Sleep on your own time.
then other: work.end

rule w7_rep_tired_boss_cold_told
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=tired pair.boss=b pair.mem.w7_from=a warmth=cold
say Tired? There's an hour yet. | I don't pay you to yawn. | Sleep on your own time.
then other: work.end

## Busy

rule w7_rep_busy
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=busy
say I'll let you get on. | Don't let me keep you. | Better busy than idle. | Rather you than me.

rule w7_rep_busy_merchant
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=busy role=merchant business!=thriving
say Lucky. My side's dead. | Send the overflow my way. | Busy? I'd take busy.

rule w7_rep_busy_failing
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=busy business=failing
priority 1
say Busy? Mine's dead as a doornail. | Send a few my way. Please. | I'd give a paw for busy.

rule w7_rep_busy_rival
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=busy pair.band=rivals
priority 1
say Busy looking busy, more like. | Don't strain yourself. | Make the most of it.

rule w7_rep_busy_idle_self
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=busy shift=day_off|after
say And here's me with my feet up. Sorry. | I'd help, but I'm enjoying watching. | Busy's good. Busy pays.

## A slack spell

rule w7_rep_idle
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=idle
say Rest while you can. | A slack spell never killed anyone. | It'll pick up. | Put your feet up, then.

rule w7_rep_idle_restless
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=idle drive=restless
say Quiet's worse than busy. I'd go mad. | I'd be climbing the walls. | Then do something else. I would.

## Bored with it

rule w7_rep_bored
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=bored
say Everyone's bored of something. | Could be worse. Could be hungry. | Find a new trade, then. | There's worse things than dull.

rule w7_rep_bored_restless
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=bored drive=restless
say Don't start me. I'd be out the gate by noon. | Me too. Shall we run off to sea? | Same. Every morning I think, one day.

rule w7_rep_bored_content
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=bored drive=content
say I like the same thing every day. Settles me. | Dull's safe. I'll take safe. | You want excitement? Try being ill.

rule w7_rep_bored_old
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=bored stage=old
say At your age I wanted the same. Then I didn't. | Dull's a luxury, #address#. You'll see. | Go and see a bit of the world, then. While you can.

rule w7_rep_bored_warm
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=bored warmth=warm
say You'll find your way. You always do. | Then try something new. I'll help. | Come and help me a day. That'll cure you.

## Denying it

rule w7_rep_proud
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=proud
say If you say so. | That's not what I heard. | Course it is. | Right you are.

rule w7_rep_proud_warm
when concept=work.reply pair.mem.w7_tone=proud warmth=warm pair.band=friends|family|spouses
say You can tell me, you know. I'll not tell a soul. | #pet.capitalize#. I've seen the shelves. | Say it as it is. It's only me.
then other: work.thanks

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- Closing

## A plain last word (work.end)

rule w7_end_plain
when concept=work.end
say Aye. Well. | Right. | Back to it, then. | #saying#. | We'll see.

rule w7_end_working
when concept=work.end working=yes shift=during
say Right. Back to it. | Better get on. | This won't do itself. | I'll get on, then.

rule w7_end_short
when concept=work.end temper=short
say Hmph. | We'll see. | If you say so.

rule w7_end_tired
when concept=work.end tired=yes
say Mm. Yes. *yawns* | Right. Right. | Mm. #bed.capitalize# soon, thank the gods.

rule w7_end_dusk
when concept=work.end here.time=dusk shift=during|after
say Nearly lamp-lighting. Nearly home. | Not long now. | One more hour. One.

## To kindness or an offer (work.thanks)

rule w7_thx_plain
when concept=work.thanks
say #thanks#. Really. | You're good to me. | I'll remember that. | That's kind. Truly.

rule w7_thx_merry
when concept=work.thanks humour=merry
say Ha! Go on with you. | You're a tonic, you are. | I'll hold you to that, mind.

rule w7_thx_quiet
when concept=work.thanks talk=quiet
say Oh. Thank you. | ...Thanks. | That's... thank you.

rule w7_thx_short
when concept=work.thanks temper=short
say Hm. Thanks. | Aye. Well. Thanks. | Don't fuss. But thanks.

rule w7_thx_tired
when concept=work.thanks tired=yes
say Mm. Thanks. I might, at that. | You're right. I know you're right. | Thanks. I'll not argue. Haven't the strength.

rule w7_thx_proud
when concept=work.thanks warmth=cold honesty=guarded|frank
priority 1
say I don't need help. I'll manage. | I'll be fine. Don't fuss. | Keep it. I'm not a charity.

rule w7_thx_young
when concept=work.thanks stage=young|adolescent
say Thank you! I mean it! | Really? Thank you! | You're the best. Don't tell anyone I said.

## To a jibe (work.retort)

rule w7_ret_plain
when concept=work.retort
say Thank you so much. | Charming. | Always a kind word from you. | Lovely to see you too.

rule w7_ret_short
when concept=work.retort temper=short
say Mind your tongue. | Say that again, slowly. | Keep your nose out of my trade.

rule w7_ret_dry
when concept=work.retort humour=dry
say Your sympathy moves me. Nearly. | I'll treasure that. | Do you practise, or does it come natural?

rule w7_ret_quiet
when concept=work.retort talk=quiet
say ... | Hm. | Mm.

rule w7_ret_rival
when concept=work.retort pair.band=rivals
say We'll see who's still open at midwinter. | Keep talking. It's all you're good for. | Wait and see. Just wait.

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- Telling, unasked (self opens with their own news)

rule w7_tell_failing
when concept=talk.work|talk.smalltalk business=failing pair.band=friends|family|spouses
cooldown 12h
say I've to tell someone. The shop's going under. | I counted the till twice this morning. It didn't help. | If nothing changes, I'm shut by the month's end.
remember pair: w7_tone=low 30m
remember pair: w7_from=a 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_tell_thriving
when concept=talk.work|talk.smalltalk business=thriving pair.band=friends|family|spouses|acquaintances
cooldown 2d
say Sold out again. Third day running. | I've had to turn folk away. Turn them away! | Best week the shop's ever had.
remember pair: w7_tone=high 30m
remember pair: w7_from=a 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_tell_boast_rival
when concept=talk.work|talk.smalltalk business=thriving pair.band=rivals
cooldown 2d
say Queue outside my door again this morning. Did you see? | Funny how folk know quality when they taste it. | I may have to hire. Business is that good.
remember pair: w7_tone=high 30m
remember pair: w7_from=a 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_tell_tired
when concept=talk.work tired=yes working=yes
cooldown 1d
say I could sleep on this bench. | If I sit, I'll grow roots. | My eyelids weigh a stone each.
remember pair: w7_tone=tired 30m
remember pair: w7_from=a 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_tell_restday
when concept=talk.work|talk.day here.day=rest working=yes
cooldown 1d
say Restday, and here we are. | Everyone at chapel but us. | I'll rest when I'm dead, apparently.
remember pair: w7_tone=hard 30m
remember pair: w7_from=a 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_tell_market_rush
when concept=talk.work here.day=market role=merchant other.role=merchant
cooldown 1d
say Market day and I've three paws too few. | I've sold more by noon than all last week. | Who are all these folk? Where do they come from?
remember pair: w7_tone=busy 30m
remember pair: w7_from=a 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_tell_owes
when concept=talk.work|talk.smalltalk owes=yes pair.band=friends|family|spouses
cooldown 12h
say Every penny I make goes to the lender. Every one. | I owe more than I'm worth. Don't tell anyone. | I lie awake doing sums.
remember pair: w7_tone=skint 30m
remember pair: w7_from=a 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_tell_apprentice_grumble
when concept=talk.work|talk.smalltalk apprentice=yes pair.boss=no
cooldown 1d
say My master had me sweep the yard three times. Three. | Five years of this before I'm my own wolf. | They shout at me for asking, then shout at me for not asking.
remember pair: w7_tone=hard 30m
remember pair: w7_from=a 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_tell_master_grumble
when concept=talk.work|talk.smalltalk master=yes pair.band!=apprentice
cooldown 1d
say My apprentice dropped a whole tray. A whole tray. | I was that clumsy once. I'm sure I wasn't. | Teaching's harder than the trade.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=a 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_tell_ambitious
when concept=talk.work|talk.smalltalk drive=ambitious business=thriving|steady pair.band=friends|acquaintances
cooldown 2d
say I'm going to buy the place next door. You watch. | One stall's a living. Two's a business. | Five years from now, my name over a proper door.
remember pair: w7_tone=good 30m
remember pair: w7_from=a 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_tell_restless
when concept=talk.work drive=restless working=yes
cooldown 2d
say I've done this same thing every day for six years. | Do you ever think of just walking out the gate? | One day I'll leave all this and go to sea.
remember pair: w7_tone=bored 30m
remember pair: w7_from=a 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_tell_content
when concept=talk.work drive=content working=yes
cooldown 2d
say Good honest work, this. I'd not swap it. | My #dad# did this, and his before him. Suits me. | There's a rhythm to it. I like the rhythm.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=a 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_tell_poor_wages
when concept=talk.work|talk.smalltalk wealth=poor|destitute working=yes
cooldown 1d
say Worked all week and I've four pennies to show. | The #wages# don't cover the rent. Not near. | Working and still hungry. How's that right?
remember pair: w7_tone=skint 30m
remember pair: w7_from=a 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_tell_old_hands
when concept=talk.work stage=old working=yes
cooldown 2d
say My paws aren't what they were, and the work doesn't care. | Forty years at this. My knees know every one. | The young ones do it faster. Not better. Faster. And I'm sore.
remember pair: w7_tone=hard 30m
remember pair: w7_from=a 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_tell_young_hand
when concept=talk.work stage=adolescent working=yes other.stage=adult|old
cooldown 2d
say Is it always this hard? | They gave me the worst job again. Because I'm new. | I did it right first time today! Nobody saw.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=a 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_tell_hurt
when concept=talk.work injured=light working=yes
cooldown 12h
say Caught my paw in it this morning. Still throbbing. | Working with a #hurt# shoulder. Don't laugh. | Pulled something lifting. Pulled everything, maybe.
remember pair: w7_tone=hard 30m
remember pair: w7_from=a 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_tell_dusk
when concept=talk.work here.time=dusk working=yes shift=during
cooldown 1d
say Light's going, and so am I. | Almost lamp-lighting. I'll not last till then. | Another hour and I'm done. If I last it.
remember pair: w7_tone=tired 30m
remember pair: w7_from=a 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_tell_dawn
when concept=talk.work here.time=dawn working=yes
cooldown 1d
say Too early for this. Far too early. | Sun's not up and nor am I, properly. | First one in again. Nobody else wants dawn.
remember pair: w7_tone=tired 30m
remember pair: w7_from=a 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_tell_rain_outdoor
when concept=talk.work here.weather=rain|storm job=farmer|laborer|woodcutter|herder|carter|fisher
cooldown 1d
say Soaked to the skin and the work's not half done. | My fur's never going to dry. | This #rain# gets in everywhere. Everywhere.
remember pair: w7_tone=hard 30m
remember pair: w7_from=a 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_tell_snow_outdoor
when concept=talk.work here.weather=snow job=farmer|laborer|woodcutter|herder|carter|guard
cooldown 1d
say Can't feel my paws. | Snow in my boots, snow in my ears. | Everything takes twice as long in this.
remember pair: w7_tone=hard 30m
remember pair: w7_from=a 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_tell_heat_forge
when concept=talk.work here.season=summer here.weather=clear job=smith|baker|cook|brewer
cooldown 1d
say Summer and a fire all day. I'm cooked. | I'm panting like a bellows. | Who wants hot work in this? Me, apparently.
remember pair: w7_tone=tired 30m
remember pair: w7_from=a 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_tell_comfortable_steady
when concept=talk.work business=steady pair.band=friends|acquaintances
cooldown 2d
say Steady week. I'll take steady. | Nothing grand, nothing awful. Paid the rent. | Regulars came, regulars paid. That's a good week.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=a 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_tell_rich_bored
when concept=talk.work|talk.smalltalk wealth=rich business=thriving|steady
cooldown 2d
say Honestly, I could stop. I just don't know what I'd do. | The ledgers keep me busier than the trade now. | I've hired another pair of paws. Strange, being the one who pays.
remember pair: w7_tone=high 30m
remember pair: w7_from=a 30m
then other: work.reply

## Broad tellings: almost anyone (few criteria)

rule w7_tell_any_plain
when concept=talk.work
cooldown 1d
say Same old, same old. | Another day, another penny. Well, half a one. | I swear the work grows when I'm not looking. | Thought I'd finish early. Thought wrong.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=a 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_tell_any_good_day
when concept=talk.work
cooldown 2d
say Good day today. Everything went right, for once. | Do you know, I think I did good work today. | Not one thing broke. Not one. I'm suspicious.
remember pair: w7_tone=good 30m
remember pair: w7_from=a 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_tell_any_bad_day
when concept=talk.work
cooldown 2d
say Everything I touched today went wrong. | One of those days. You know the sort. | If the morning's anything to go by, I should go home now.
remember pair: w7_tone=hard 30m
remember pair: w7_from=a 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_tell_any_tools
when concept=talk.work stage=adult|old
cooldown 2d
say Broke my best tool today. Twenty years I had it. | Someone's moved my things again. Nobody admits it. | New tool. Stiff as a board. It'll learn.
remember pair: w7_tone=hard 30m
remember pair: w7_from=a 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_tell_any_customer
when concept=talk.work stage=adult|old business=thriving|steady|failing
cooldown 2d
say Had a customer today who wanted it cheaper, quicker and better. Pick two, I said. | Somebody paid me in buttons. Buttons! | A pup came in and asked if I was rich. I laughed for an hour.
remember pair: w7_tone=plain 30m
remember pair: w7_from=a 30m
then other: work.reply

rule w7_tell_any_weekend
when concept=talk.work here.day=work
cooldown 2d
say How many days to Restday? Don't tell me. I'll cry. | I'm counting the hours to Restday. I'm that worn. | Restday can't come soon enough. I'm dead on my paws.
remember pair: w7_tone=tired 30m
remember pair: w7_from=a 30m
then other: work.reply

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- The boss and the hand

rule w7_boss_order
when concept=talk.work pair.boss=a other.working=yes self.temper=calm|even
cooldown 1d
say When you're done there, the yard wants sweeping. | Leave that. I need you out front today. | Take your time with it. Do it right.
then other: work.order

rule w7_boss_order_short
when concept=talk.work pair.boss=a other.working=yes self.temper=short|nervy
cooldown 1d
say Faster. We're behind. | Not like that. Like I showed you. | I wanted that done an hour ago.
then other: work.order

rule w7_boss_order_market
when concept=talk.work pair.boss=a here.day=market self.role=merchant
cooldown 1d
say Market day. Smile at everyone. Even the ones who don't buy. | Watch the front. Watch the pockets. | Stack them high. Folk buy what looks plenty.
then other: work.order

rule w7_boss_order_failing
when concept=talk.work pair.boss=a self.business=failing
cooldown 1d
say Mind the waste. Every scrap counts now. | Go easy on the lamp oil. We're tightening belts a while. | Don't light the second lamp. We can't spare it.
then other: work.order

rule w7_boss_scold_cold
when concept=talk.work pair.boss=a self.warmth=cold other.tired=yes
cooldown 1d
say You're dragging your tail. | Are you working or dreaming? | If you're tired, there's others who'd want your place.
then other: work.order

rule w7_boss_order_thriving
when concept=talk.work pair.boss=a self.business=thriving self.warmth=warm
cooldown 2d
say Good work this week. I mean that. | We're doing well. You've helped. | Keep this up and we'll talk about your #wages#.
then other: work.praised

rule w7_boss_praise_warm
when concept=talk.work pair.boss=a self.warmth=warm other.working=yes
cooldown 2d
say That's good work. Neat. | You've a knack for that. | I'd not have done it better myself.
then other: work.praised

rule w7_worker_asks_wage
when concept=talk.work pair.boss=b self.wealth=poor|destitute
cooldown 1d
say Any chance of my #wages# early? Just this once. | The rent's due. Could you pay me a few days ahead? | Could I have what I've earned so far?
then other: work.plea

rule w7_worker_asks_raise
when concept=talk.work pair.boss=b self.drive=ambitious
cooldown 3d
say I've been here long enough to earn a bit more. | I do the work of two. Pay me for one and a half? | Others pay better, you know. I've stayed.
then other: work.plea

rule w7_worker_asks_rest
when concept=talk.work pair.boss=b self.tired=yes
cooldown 1d
say Could I knock off early? I'm dead on my paws. | Can I sit a moment? Just a moment. | Can I go home early? I'll come in at dawn.
then other: work.leave

rule w7_worker_asks_festival
when concept=talk.work pair.boss=b world.festival=soon
cooldown 2d
say Can I have the festival day? My family's expecting me. | Could I have the festival evening off? Just the evening. | I'd work the festival, if you paid double. Or have it off, if you didn't.
then other: work.leave

rule w7_worker_asks_late_pay
when concept=talk.work pair.boss=b other.business=failing
cooldown 1d
say I've not been paid this week. | Will there be #wages# on Restday? | Folk are saying the shop's in trouble. Is it?
then other: work.worry

## The hand answers an order or a scolding (work.order)

rule w7_ord_plain
when concept=work.order
say Right away. | Aye. On it. | I'll see to it. | Yes, all right.
then other: work.end

rule w7_ord_short
when concept=work.order temper=short
say I'm doing it. | Yes, yes. | I heard you the first time.
then other: work.end

rule w7_ord_tired
when concept=work.order tired=yes
say Yes. Right. In a moment. | If my legs agree. | ...Yes. Sorry. Yes.
then other: work.end

rule w7_ord_merry
when concept=work.order humour=merry
say At once, your lordship! | Your wish, my command. My aching command. | Right you are. I'll whistle while I do it, to annoy you.

rule w7_ord_ambitious
when concept=work.order drive=ambitious
say Leave it with me. And the rest, if you like. | I'll have it done before you're back. Then give me something harder. | Consider it done. What's next?

rule w7_ord_sly
when concept=work.order honesty=sly
say Of course. Who'd notice if I took a little longer? | Yes, yes. Will you be watching? | Right away. More or less.
then other: work.end

rule w7_ord_apprentice
when concept=work.order apprentice=yes
say Yes, master. | Like this? Is this right? | I'll get it right this time. I will.
then other: work.end

rule w7_ord_young
when concept=work.order stage=adolescent
say Why is it always me? ...Fine. | Fine. But I'm doing the good bit after. | Can't someone else? ...Fine.

## The hand takes praise (work.praised)

rule w7_prz_plain
when concept=work.praised
say Thank you. That means something. | I've been trying. | Kind of you to say.

rule w7_prz_cold
when concept=work.praised warmth=cold
say About time someone noticed. | I know. | It's what you pay me for.

rule w7_prz_quiet
when concept=work.praised talk=quiet
say Oh. Thank you. | ...Thanks. | Mm. Glad it's right.

rule w7_prz_merry
when concept=work.praised humour=merry
say Write it down somewhere. I'll want proof. | Say it louder. The others can't hear. | I'm wonderful. I keep telling everyone.

rule w7_prz_ambitious
when concept=work.praised drive=ambitious
say Then perhaps we could talk about my #wages#? | Good enough for a bit more, would you say? | Then give me more of it. And pay me for it.
then other: work.plea

rule w7_prz_sly
when concept=work.praised honesty=sly
say Praise is lovely. Coin's lovelier. | Lovely. Does it come with anything? | I'll frame it. Next to my empty purse.
then other: work.plea

rule w7_prz_apprentice
when concept=work.praised apprentice=yes
say Thank you, master. I'll keep at it. | Really? I thought I'd spoiled it. | I watched you do it. That's all.

rule w7_prz_young
when concept=work.praised stage=adolescent
say Really? You mean it? | Nobody's said that before. | Wait till I tell #mum#.

rule w7_prz_tired
when concept=work.praised tired=yes
say Thanks. I'd be prouder awake. | Mm. Good. Can I sit down now? | Thank you. It nearly killed me.

## The boss answers a plea for pay (work.plea)

rule w7_plea_plain
when concept=work.plea
say We'll see. | Let me think on it. | Not this week. Ask me again. | Perhaps.
then other: work.end

rule w7_plea_warm
when concept=work.plea warmth=warm
say Go on, then. Just this once. | Fair's fair. You've earned it. | I'll see you right. I promise.
then other: work.thanks

rule w7_plea_cold
when concept=work.plea warmth=cold
say No. | You'll get what you're owed when it's owed. | If you don't like it, there's the door.
then other: work.end

rule w7_plea_failing
when concept=work.plea business=failing
priority 1
say There's nothing to give. I'm sorry. Truly. | I'm paying you before I pay myself, as it is. | If it picks up. If.
then other: work.end

rule w7_plea_thriving_warm
when concept=work.plea business=thriving warmth=warm
priority 1
say Fair's fair. A bit more from next week. | Business is good. You'll see some of it. | I'll not forget who carried the load.
then other: work.thanks

rule w7_plea_thriving_cold
when concept=work.plea business=thriving warmth=cold
priority 1
say Good trade is my reward for my risk. Not yours. | We'll see how the month ends. | You're paid what we agreed.
then other: work.end

rule w7_plea_short
when concept=work.plea temper=short
say Don't push your luck. | Ask me again and I'll halve it. | Back to work.
then other: work.end

rule w7_plea_sly
when concept=work.plea honesty=sly
say Course. Next week. Definitely next week. | Remind me Restday. I'll have forgotten, mind. | Leave it with me. I'll see what I can see.
then other: work.end

rule w7_plea_rich
when concept=work.plea wealth=rich warmth!=cold
say Here. Don't make a habit of it. | Fine. I can spare it. | Go on. I'll not miss it.
then other: work.thanks

rule w7_plea_poor_boss
when concept=work.plea wealth=poor|destitute
say With what? I've less than you. | I'd pay you if I could pay me. | Look in the till. Go on, look.
then other: work.end

## The boss answers a plea for time off (work.leave)

rule w7_leave_plain
when concept=work.leave
say We'll see how the day goes. | If the work's done, yes. | Not today. Tomorrow, maybe.
then other: work.end

rule w7_leave_warm
when concept=work.leave warmth=warm
say Go on. I'll manage. | Of course. Take it. | You've earned a rest. Go.
then other: work.thanks

rule w7_leave_cold
when concept=work.leave warmth=cold
say No. There's work to do. | Rest on your own time. | You'll have it when everyone has it.
then other: work.end

rule w7_leave_short
when concept=work.leave temper=short
say Don't push it. | Ask me when it's done. | No. Back to it.
then other: work.end

rule w7_leave_thriving
when concept=work.leave business=thriving warmth!=warm
priority 1
say Not now. Look at the queue. | When the rush is over. Not before. | We're run off our paws. Later.
then other: work.end

rule w7_leave_failing
when concept=work.leave business=failing
priority 1
say Take it. There's little enough to do. | Go. I can't pay for idle hours anyway. | Have it. Have two, if you like. Nobody's buying.
then other: work.thanks

rule w7_leave_devout_restday
when concept=work.leave piety=devout here.day=rest
priority 1
say It's Restday. Go. Go home. I shouldn't have kept you. | Go to chapel. The work can wait for the Bright One. | Of course. Rest. It's what the day's for.
then other: work.thanks

## The boss answers a worry about the shop and the pay (work.worry)

rule w7_worry_plain
when concept=work.worry
say You'll be paid. You always have been. | Don't listen to gossip. | We'll pull through. We always do.
then other: work.end

rule w7_worry_failing
when concept=work.worry business=failing
priority 1
say I'll not lie to you. It's bad. | Pay might be late. It won't be missed. Not while I've breath. | If it comes to letting you go, you'll hear it from me first.
then other: work.end

rule w7_worry_thriving
when concept=work.worry business=thriving
priority 1
say Trouble? We've never been busier. | Safe as the walls. Who's been saying otherwise? | Your #wages# are the last thing you need fret about.
then other: work.end

rule w7_worry_warm
when concept=work.worry warmth=warm
say Whatever happens, you'll not go hungry. I promise you that. | Come here. Listen. We'll manage, the two of us. | I'll look after you. I always have.
then other: work.thanks

rule w7_worry_cold
when concept=work.worry warmth=cold
say That's my business. Get back to work. | Worry about your work. I'll worry about the till. | If you want to go, go.
then other: work.end

rule w7_worry_sly
when concept=work.worry honesty=sly
say Safe as houses. Don't ask again. | Trouble? Never heard of it. | Who told you that? Never mind. It's nothing.
then other: work.end
